A||||9||MooCow||My car will not stay started in the morning!||||8||
Z||000000||MooCow||08-12-2000||11:58 PM||||OOOOO  Every morning when I start my car up it will never stay started.  It will start then die.  I have to keep revving it or it will die. I keep it reved at 2 grand for about a 45-60 seconds then let go of the gas and then it will idle correctly and stay started. What to do??? Check the spark plugs possibly?? Change my ideling to higher??<BR>All info will help out.<P>                                Thanks Ken||||reg||8
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-13-2000||04:01 AM||||If you're EGR selenoid is not connected properly, you'll have those symptoms... Had them on two Fiero's.  It's that cylindrical black object on the right side of the intake.  It has several vacuum lines connected to it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||08-13-2000||06:22 AM||||Mines been sounding like it's going to start doing this soon as well. I starts up nice and idles fine for the first 10/15 seconds, then starts to bog down like it's going to die out then revs back up again. It does this 3 or 4 times them just starts to idle again. Bad IAC valve? Maybe I used too much of Ed Parks' de-carbonizing spray down into the throttle body hole where the pindle of the IAC is? I noticed after applying it she would idle aroung 2000rpm instead of the normal 900/1000 for the first day. I thought I was going to have to replace the valve but it started idleing around 900 again but I'm getting the "bogging down" symptons I mentioned above. My EGR solenoid is hooked up properly and is only 3 months old!<P>Marc 87GT<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 08-13-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||Fformula88||08-13-2000||12:18 PM||||I have been battling this problem for a while now.  It had gotten so bad at one point that the car would bog down at stop signs and lights for about the first five minutes it was running, and then it would be fine.  I tried a tune up, replacing all the filters etc etc and that didn't clear up the problem.  The car did run a lot better overall!  I also had a couple vacumn leaks, so after some new vacumn lines and an EGR tube, it got a little better.  What seemed to help the most was spraying a can of carb cleaner into the Throttle body while the car was running.  I got an extra big can and just kept spraying the whole thing in.  This helped a LOT.  Now, when I start it, the revs go up, then it starts to bog.  If I tap the throttle they go back up and stay up.  I can live with that so I haven't tried anything else.  Hope this helps some!  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||08-14-2000||12:35 AM||||Bad cold start injector maybe??||||reg||1
Z||000005||trigger||08-16-2000||07:24 PM||||My 88 coupe 2.5 auto did the same thing until i changed the electronic spark advance and fixed the oxygen sensor.  Sensor was unplugged.<P>P.S.  How come I can't post smilies in my message.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000006||otis||08-18-2000||02:10 PM||||I have the same symptoms as posted<BR>by moo. I think the tps and the<BR>temp sensors come into play on<BR>startup. Does the ecm have any<BR>stored data that could  become<BR>corrupted and cause this problem<BR>as well? I will change my tps sensor<BR>and then if no luck maybe a used<BR>ecm with chip from Ed Parks.||||reg||8
Z||000007||JohnnyK||08-18-2000||02:14 PM||||Mine does this, and I have no idea what causes this. It will rev at 1000 for a few seconds, and then drop to 500 and struggle, and then up to 1000, and then down to 500 and struggle, etc, etc, but it's usually (I think) in rhythm. Say, 1000 for 5 seconds, 500 for 2, 1000 for 5, etc. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||ROB MAC||08-18-2000||03:51 PM||||First time mine did that it was a faulty isolation relay but, it ran kinda crummy all the time. Recently my cold start idle problem was fixed by switching back to solid old style V-belt instead of the "ribbed" or "toothed" belts that stretch easy and slip. The last belt stretched so much I couldn't tighten it any more and it was less than a year old. Remember, new belts will stretch a little so check them occasionally.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Seanh||08-18-2000||04:54 PM||||My car does the same thing. I start it up in the morning and it does fine when I start it and then It drops down in RPM's and struggles, but never dies. When I get in to drive it alot, after I first start it up, I wont have much acceleration and it seems no matter how far I push the gas pedel, the engine dosent increase in RPM's then pretty soon the car will just take off, and run great all the way to work. Any Ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
